WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:19.907
"Gum?" Cole said in surprise. "Are you sure that's all that's in there?"

2
00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:24.436
"Yeah," said Maggie. "Is our next clue in there?"

3
00:00:24.437 --> 00:00:29.390
"Um . . . let's see." Luke turned the container upside down and shook it.

4
00:00:29.391 --> 00:00:33.883
Some tissue paper fluttered out. Then a folded piece of paper fell out.

5
00:00:33.884 --> 00:00:37.981
Maggie picked up the folded paper. "It's another clue.

6
00:00:37.982 --> 00:00:41.743
So this is definitely the right box," she said.

7
00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:46.572
"Hey, William, why would your parents give us a few lousy sticks of gum?

8
00:00:46.573 --> 00:00:48.732
That's not much of a treasure."

9
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:52.746
"Shh," Henry shushed her. Maggie was being rude.

10
00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:58.256
"It is kind of weird," Cole said. "Do pirates even chew gum?"

11
00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:02.100
Nathan shrugged. "I don't think so," he said.

12
00:01:02.101 --> 00:01:05.239
"I doubt they can get it on the high seas."

13
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.422
Luke laughed. "Maybe they steal it from the ships they raid."

14
00:01:09.423 --> 00:01:13.301
He tilted his pirate hat and then pretended to swing his sword.

15
00:01:13.302 --> 00:01:18.617
"Ahoy, mateys! Give me your gum, or I'll make you walk the plank!"

16
00:01:18.618 --> 00:01:22.376
Nathan pretended to fight back with an invisible sword.

17
00:01:22.377 --> 00:01:28.505
"No way!" he cried. "I'll die before I hand over my gum!"

18
00:01:28.506 --> 00:01:32.053
"Stop messing around, you guys," Maggie said.

19
00:01:32.054 --> 00:01:36.048
"Seriously, why would William's parents give us gum?

20
00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:39.142
It doesn't fit in with the pirate theme at all."

21
00:01:39.143 --> 00:01:42.624
Henry didn't say anything, but he had to agree.

22
00:01:42.625 --> 00:01:48.300
"Oh well." Cole grabbed one of the sticks of gum.

23
00:01:48.301 --> 00:01:51.736
"At least we can chew gum while we follow the next clue."

24
00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:54.585
Then he looked at the gum and wrinkled his nose.

25
00:01:54.586 --> 00:02:01.891
"Yuck," he added. "Never mind. It's watermelon. I hate that flavor."

26
00:02:01.892 --> 00:02:06.294
"Watermelon? Cool!" Luke grabbed another stick of gum.

27
00:02:06.295 --> 00:02:11.787
"That's my favorite. I buy this gum at the general store every time I come here.

28
00:02:11.788 --> 00:02:15.589
Anna's store is the only place I know that sells this brand."

29
00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:20.027
"Your family owns a general store?" Maggie asked Anna.

30
00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:25.633
"Great deduction, detective Maggie," Nathan said sarcastically.

31
00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:28.281
Henry was surprised by Nathan's remark.

32
00:02:28.282 --> 00:02:34.302
"Is Nathan still mad at Maggie for grabbing the map away from him earlier?" Henry thought.

33
00:02:34.303 --> 00:02:36.194
That wasn't like Nathan at all.

34
00:02:36.195 --> 00:02:41.436
He almost never got mad. And even if he did, he didn't stay mad for long.

35
00:02:41.437 --> 00:02:46.974
"My family's store is one of the oldest businesses in Sea Cove," Anna told Maggie.

36
00:02:46.975 --> 00:02:50.430
"My great-grandfather started the store a long time ago.

37
00:02:50.431 --> 00:02:52.991
Everyone in town shops there."

38
00:02:52.992 --> 00:03:00.122
Luke grinned and blew a bubble. "Yeah. They have the best gum in town!"

39
00:03:00.123 --> 00:03:03.906
Cole tossed his gum back into the container.

40
00:03:03.907 --> 00:03:08.865
"I still think a few sticks of gum is a weird prize," he said.

41
00:03:08.866 --> 00:03:11.210
"Especially for a pirate treasure hunt.

42
00:03:11.211 --> 00:03:13.783
Are you sure we found the right box, William?"

43
00:03:13.784 --> 00:03:17.568
"How should I know?" William snapped with a frown.

44
00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:21.476
"I didn't have anything to do with this stupid scavenger hunt."

45
00:03:21.477 --> 00:03:25.575
Cole looked surprised. "Okay," he said.

46
00:03:25.576 --> 00:03:29.982
Henry bit his lip. Everyone seemed a little grouchy right now.

47
00:03:29.983 --> 00:03:34.056
"Why don't we go see if lunch is ready?" he suggested.

48
00:03:34.057 --> 00:03:37.538
"Maybe we can ask William's parents about the gum."

49
00:03:37.539 --> 00:03:47.877
"Good idea," Cole agreed. "All this treasure hunting has made me hungry."

50
00:03:47.878 --> 00:03:49.728
They headed back to the house.

51
00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.171
A lunch of sandwiches and juice was set out on the deck.

52
00:03:53.172 --> 00:03:57.658
William's parents were there too, sipping tall glasses of iced tea.

53
00:03:57.659 --> 00:04:03.279
As the kids sat down to eat, they told William's parents about how the treasure hunt was going so far.

54
00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.660
When they got to the part about the gum, William's mother looked surprised.

55
00:04:07.661 --> 00:04:12.170
"Gum?" she said. "I didn't put any gum in the box."

56
00:04:12.171 --> 00:04:16.189
Maggie nodded. "The next clue was in the box too."

57
00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:19.587
She took the piece of paper out of her shorts pocket and held it up.

58
00:04:19.588 --> 00:04:22.466
William's parents traded a confused look.

59
00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:27.215
"Are you sure there wasn't a white envelope in the box too?" William's father asked.

60
00:04:27.216 --> 00:04:29.821
"We're sure," Henry said.

61
00:04:29.822 --> 00:04:35.646
"There was nothing inside except the clue, some tissue paper, and a few sticks of gum."

62
00:04:35.647 --> 00:04:39.299
"What was in the envelope?" Luke asked William's parents.

63
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.966
"Your booty," William's father answered.

64
00:04:41.967 --> 00:04:44.924
"Seven movie tickets—one for each of you."

65
00:04:44.925 --> 00:04:48.182
"Movie tickets?" Maggie said.

66
00:04:48.183 --> 00:04:53.914
William's mother nodded. "Not just ordinary movie tickets, either," she said.

67
00:04:53.915 --> 00:04:58.006
"They were for the local premiere of Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost."

68
00:04:58.007 --> 00:04:59.688
The kids gasped.

69
00:04:59.689 --> 00:05:04.189
That was the title of the new pirate movie that was coming out next month.

70
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:10.077
"Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost?" Nathan cried. "I'm dying to see that!"

71
00:05:10.078 --> 00:05:13.566
"You know what this means, don't you?" Maggie said.

72
00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:15.779
"What?" Luke asked.

73
00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:21.156
"Someone stole our pirate booty." Maggie glanced at Henry and Cole.

74
00:05:21.157 --> 00:05:26.022
"This is a job for The Lemonade Detectives!"
